{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:113-114", "row": 15, "speaker": "قيل", "claim": "Another interpretation is do not ask for revelation before it comes to you."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:113-114", "row": 17, "speaker": "الحسن", "claim": "Al-Ḥasan says the passage was revealed about a man who slapped his wife; after the Prophet granted her retaliation, 4:34 was revealed."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:113-114", "row": 18, "speaker": "الحسن", "claim": "In al-Ḥasan's account, increased knowledge means understanding, since God corrected the Prophet's ruling on retaliation."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:113-114", "row": 19, "speaker": "author", "claim": "The prayer asks God to increase the Prophet's understanding."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:113-114", "row": 20, "speaker": "ابن مسعود وغيره", "claim": "Ibn Masʿūd and others read من قبل أن نقضي with nūn, a kasra on ḍād, and وحيه in the accusative."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:115", "row": 1, "speaker": "الأعمش", "claim": "Al-Aʿmash has a variant reading of فنسي with the yāʾ quiescent."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:115", "row": 3, "speaker": "ابن عباس", "claim": "Ibn ʿAbbās takes نسي as genuine forgetfulness: a human was made from a covenant he then forgot."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:115", "row": 4, "speaker": "ابن زيد", "claim": "Ibn Zayd says Adam forgot God's charge; had he been firm, he would not have obeyed Iblīs."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:115", "row": 6, "speaker": "author", "claim": "من قبل means before Adam ate from the forbidden tree."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:115", "row": 7, "speaker": "القشيري والطبري", "claim": "Al-Qushayrī and al-Ṭabarī present the passage as consolation for the Prophet: human obedience to Satan is ancient, and Adam too broke a charge."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:115", "row": 8, "speaker": "ابن عطية", "claim": "Ibn ʿAṭiyya rejects making Adam a model for unbelievers who knowingly deny God: Adam sinned through interpretation, so the comparison is weak and dishonors the Prophet."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:115", "row": 9, "speaker": "ابن عطية", "claim": "Ibn ʿAṭiyya prefers either a fresh narrative or a link to the Prophet's command not to hasten revelation: Adam's forgotten charge warns him more strongly."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:115", "row": 11, "speaker": "ابن عطية", "claim": "Ibn ʿAṭiyya takes نسي as leaving the command, not absent-minded forgetting, since such forgetfulness cannot incur punishment."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:115", "row": 13, "speaker": "author", "claim": "The charge was not to eat from the tree, and Adam was warned that Iblīs was his enemy."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:115#2", "row": 1, "speaker": "ابن عباس وقتادة", "claim": "Ibn ʿAbbās and Qatāda explain the lack of resolve as lack of patience resisting the tree and steadiness in keeping the command."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:115#2", "row": 2, "speaker": "النحاس", "claim": "Al-Naḥḥās says عزم linguistically means patience and firmness in guarding oneself from sin; he links it to 46:35."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:115#2", "row": 4, "speaker": "ابن عباس وعطية العوفي", "claim": "On their account, Satan promised the named tree would grant eternity; Adam refused it but did not infer the similar tree was also forbidden."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:115#2", "row": 5, "speaker": "ابن عباس وعطية العوفي", "claim": "They say Adam forgot by losing knowledge through failure to reason; one who knows an act is sinful cannot forget it."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:115#2", "row": 6, "speaker": "ابن زيد", "claim": "Ibn Zayd explains عزم as preserving God's command."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:115#2", "row": 10, "speaker": "قيل", "claim": "Some infer that Adam was not among the messengers of resolve because God says He found no resolve in him."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:115#2", "row": 12, "speaker": "النبي", "claim": "A report says every prophet erred or considered a sin except Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā; excluding Adam would therefore exclude all but Yaḥyā."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:116-119", "row": 1, "speaker": "author", "claim": "The account of the angels' prostration and Iblīs's refusal was fully discussed under al-Baqara 2:34."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:116-119", "row": 3, "speaker": "author", "claim": "The singular hardship includes Adam and his wife because their cause is the same; Adam is grammatically addressed and intended."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:116-119", "row": 5, "speaker": "قيل", "claim": "Another view says both were expelled but bodily hardship is assigned only to Adam, as clarified by the following descriptions of garden life."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:116-119", "row": 7, "speaker": "author", "claim": "The singular wording teaches that a husband's maintenance is owed to his wife; the four necessities are food, drink, clothing, and housing."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:116-119", "row": 9, "speaker": "الحسن", "claim": "Al-Ḥasan takes Adam's hardship to mean worldly hardship, since no human lives without toil."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:116-119", "row": 11, "speaker": "سعيد بن جبير", "claim": "Saʿīd ibn Jubayr says Adam was sent down a red ox to plow with and wipe sweat from his brow; this was his hardship."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:116-119", "row": 14, "speaker": "author", "claim": "ظَمَأ means thirst."}
{"loc": "QURTUBI-FULL:20:116-119", "row": 15, "speaker": "author", "claim": "تضحى means exposure to the sun's heat; Paradise has no sun, only extended shade between dawn and sunrise."}
